# Ford Zephyr Mk I (Zephyr Six) four-door saloon, 1951-1956.
#
# The six-cylinder member of the 1951 range: a Consul with a four-inch longer
# bonnet and the 2,262 cc six. Six-light cabin, waist-level chrome strip and
# rounded boot. The Abbott estate and Carbodies convertible are different
# bodies and are not modelled.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ford_Zephyr
#
# Dimensions 4.369 x 1.626 x 1.524 m, wheelbase 2.642 m.
#
# Shape reference: a teal-blue Zephyr Six in true level side elevation, a
# 1953 car in front three-quarter, and a third car in rear three-quarter.
# The long bonnet and six-light cabin govern.
#
# Colours: grade (a), the period Ford dealer leaflet 'Ford Sets The Fashion'
# (1953-54 season), which names the Zephyr Six saloon colours: Opal,
# Edinburgh Green, Bristol Fawn, Dorchester Grey, Canterbury Green,
# Winchester Blue and Black. Four are used. Weights 15, 13, 12, 10, total
# 50, provisional.
#
# Speed 135 km/h. Comfort 55/413, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 55. Classes 2,3.
# Dates are road presence: 1950 intro, retires staggered 1970-1973.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/ford-zephyr-mk1.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/ford-zephyr-mk1.dae. References:
# citycars/references/ford-zephyr-mk1/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the roof corners, rear glass and bumper wrap are
# simplified. The three photographs show different cars. At 128 px the long
# bonnet, six-light cabin and rounded boot read as a Zephyr Mk I.


obj=citycar
